{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T00:39:15.975Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d97cc75851de74b9275ff63","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-08T00:39:15.975Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Evidence for the release-time check (2026-11-08): pm-8s53lj and pm-hka7ep change the public SDK contract in the next Unreleased window. Before: comment, note and learning rows carried only their stored fields, a bounded comments or notes read kept the oldest rows, learnings had no output ceiling, and PmReadOutputCursorEnvelope continued forward only. After: every listing row leads with index (IndexedAnnotationEntry), the annotation command options accept expectAt for edit and delete, learnings joins PM_READ_OUTPUT_SURFACES, bounded annotation reads keep the newest rows and continue through a cursor with direction backward, and sliceReadOutputRowCollection takes an optional end. Migrate: address entries by row.index instead of array position, follow next_cursor for older entries, and accept the optional direction field when decoding cursors. The sdk/public-surface.json acknowledgment carries the same line.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T00:39:15.975Z"}],"before_hash":"037a25b81a2cfa84647ad5d8049133acad5854ce76395c821a54d86d2533d461","after_hash":"2f0ac233d9f0fbe7f630b2f852adcf0c2258fe1e7df5a2a67b026fc3336f7de8","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"562fe4f2e2daca8538110024138f0f3e42f8040f8574240a5ade77cb29107b4f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T02:52:23.428Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d97cc75851de74b9275ff63","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-08T02:52:23.427Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Addendum (2026-11-08) to the pm-8s53lj contract line, from the PR 1685 review follow-up. Before: PmReadOutputSurfaceContract.budget_retention_policy was ordered_prefix or verdict_priority, and PmReadOutputTailRetentionPolicy declared only paths and total_key. After: comments, notes and learnings declare ordered_suffix, and a tail policy may declare delivered_row_counters (notes recount structured_event_count from the delivered rows); PmReadOutputDeliveredRowCounter is a new public type. Migrate: treat ordered_suffix as newest-first retention, and accept the optional delivered_row_counters field. The sdk/public-surface.json acknowledgment carries the same line.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T02:52:23.428Z"}],"before_hash":"2f0ac233d9f0fbe7f630b2f852adcf0c2258fe1e7df5a2a67b026fc3336f7de8","after_hash":"f49dcea1b29938090e37fa45a70747a314e1373da6be7f202fe68bc37038e392","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fa4a0a498e99980a07c86cecec5a9234edd37532323b14c38153d51f21c42c09"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-08T05:08:30.127Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d97cc75851de74b9275ff63","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_edit","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/3/text","value":"Addendum (2026-11-08) to the pm-8s53lj contract line, from the PR 1685 review follow-up. Before: PmReadOutputSurfaceContract.budget_retention_policy was ordered_prefix or verdict_priority, and PmReadOutputTailRetentionPolicy declared only paths and total_key. After: comments, notes and learnings declare ordered_suffix, and a tail policy may declare delivered_row_counters (notes recount structured_event_count from the delivered rows); PmReadOutputDeliveredRowCounter is a new public type. Migrate: treat ordered_suffix as retaining the newest rows, still listed oldest to newest within each page, and accept the optional delivered_row_counters field. The sdk/public-surface.json acknowledgment carries the same line."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3/edited_at","value":"2026-11-08T05:08:30.127Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-08T05:08:30.127Z"}],"before_hash":"f49dcea1b29938090e37fa45a70747a314e1373da6be7f202fe68bc37038e392","after_hash":"c4a022c00a907dcf6b37db8d693aec38bfef8338274c4a187c9d9fdc2efb9e71","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8330a734de9d23cb553340bf270cceff0d7e881db670b66498e432ff6a7f87e7"}
